date per tick uses the same order, so a P0 PR does not wait behind a P3 branch update.\n\n**Starvation warning**\n- Strict priority, no aging. But a grant clears `starved[class]` (`pool.go`, grant path), so a long-waiting P3 would re-warn `pool.starved` on every grant in its class. Clear the flag only when the class has no wait older than the threshold, and log the key and priority with the warning.\n\n**Proposal:** the label list and table, the \"One pool of job slots\" paragraph (\"Within a class, `ard:p0`..`ard:p3` order candidates (unlabelled = P2, several = highest), then oldest. Priority never crosses classes.\"), the merger section (\"highest priority, then lowest number\"), and the stale-closer and scanner-grouping notes.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TbW96sfUkka3i6wCuwb3Sf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
